      "id": "120",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 120,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "The past form of う-Verbs expresses a completed action or an event that took place in the past, similar to the English '-ed.' In contrast, だった and でした are used after nouns to express the past tense, indicating that something 'was' or 'were' in a certain state. While the meaning (something happened or existed in the past) is the same, the grammatical expression differs depending on the word type (verb vs. noun).",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 40,
          "slug": "だった-でした",
          "title": "だった・でした",
          "meaning": "Was, Were (Past tense) ",
          "level": "JLPT5",
